%% ===== Level 1 DFD: Existing Manual System — Registrar (new, 2026-10-30) =====
%% Decomposes the Registrar side of Figure 2.6's single manual process.
%% ---
%% The Registrar is MISSING from the published Figure 2.6, which shows only Student, Faculty and
%% Dean. The role already exists at DYCI and already does this work on paper; the proposed system
%% gives it a portal rather than inventing it.
%% ---
%% Against the proposed Registrar Portal DFD, the contrasts worth reading off this figure:
%%   - the subject catalogue, section lists and term calendar live in separate files that are
%%     re-typed into every document that needs them
%%   - enrolment is a list; a student added to a class outside their block is a handwritten note
%%   - a late grade change has no window and no authority recorded, only a signature
%%   - nothing connects a released grade to the sheet it came from
%% ---
%% Layout: External entity (left) -> Process (middle) -> Data store (right)

%% COLUMN A of 2. Split from Figure-2.6d-DFD-Existing-Registrar.mmd so the figure fits a page; compose with
%% compose_columns.py. Edit the halves, not a merged copy.
  %% ---------- 1.0 ----------
  R1["Registrar"] <-- "enrolment forms /<br/>official enrolment list" --> P1(("1.0<br/>Enrol Students<br/>and Build Sections"))
  P1 <-- "names typed into a section list" --> D8@{ shape: lin-rect, label: "D8&nbsp; Enrolment and<br/>section lists (files)" }
  P1 <-- "irregular students written in by hand" --> D9@{ shape: lin-rect, label: "D9&nbsp; Handwritten roster notes" }

  %% ---------- 2.0 ----------
  R2["Registrar"] <-- "curriculum and offerings /<br/>subject catalogue, printed" --> P2(("2.0<br/>Maintain the<br/>Subject Catalogue"))
  P2 <-- "codes, titles, units, re-typed<br/>into each document that needs them" --> D10@{ shape: lin-rect, label: "D10&nbsp; Subject and program files" }

  %% ---------- 3.0 ----------
  R3["Registrar"] <-- "academic calendar /<br/>term dates circulated on paper" --> P3(("3.0<br/>Open and Close<br/>Academic Terms"))
  P3 <-- "school year and semester,<br/>with no system to enforce them" --> D11@{ shape: lin-rect, label: "D11&nbsp; Academic calendar file" }

